# --- the new file ---
# AnixOps Control configuration, written by `anix-control config rewrite`
# from /opt/anixops/control/config/config.yaml on 2026-10-13T08:00:00Z.
# Keys and defaults: docs/reference/configuration.md. The root key and the
# secrets it adopted are in data_dir/root.key, not in this file.
domain: your-domain.com
tls:
  mode: external
  cert_file: config/tls/control.crt
  key_file: config/tls/control.key
# Still read until PostgreSQL support ends (M2, P4): the panel keeps its
# database (a PostgreSQL password stays here until then).
database:
  conn_max_lifetime: 3600
  database: "anix_control"
  driver: "postgres"
  host: "127.0.0.1"
  log_level: "error"
  max_idle_conns: 10
  max_open_conns: 100
  password: "your-secure-password"
  port: 5432
  username: "anix_control"
# --- the report ---
New keys:
  domain: your-domain.com (from tls.domain); the panel's name
  tls.mode: external
  tls.cert_file: config/tls/control.crt (from grpc.tls_cert_file)
  tls.key_file: config/tls/control.key (from grpc.tls_key_file)

Kept:
  database: still read until PostgreSQL support ends (M2, P4): the panel keeps its database

Dropped:
  admin.email: the first administrator claims the panel with a one-time link (anix-control admin claim-link); existing administrators are not affected
  admin.password: no administrator password is configured any more; the first administrator claims the panel with a one-time link (anix-control admin claim-link) and existing administrators keep theirs, so remove it
  agent_control.mtls: fixed to required, the 4.2 default; the other modes are removed with the legacy Agent transports
  app.api_token: the legacy shared token of /flow/upload and the internal v2 routes, which are removed; the key does nothing, so remove it (administrators use admin API tokens)
  app.edition: there are no editions; orders, payments and affiliate are built in
  app.name: nothing reads it
  app.subscribe_path: the default (s)
  app.traffic_log_enable: nothing reads it
  app.version: nothing reads it; the version is the binary's
  auth.login_rate_limit.enabled: login rate limiting is always on
  auth.login_rate_limit.lockout_seconds: a built-in value (600)
  auth.login_rate_limit.max_attempts: a built-in value (6)
  auth.login_rate_limit.window_seconds: a built-in value (300)
  auth.register_rate_limit.enabled: registration rate limiting is always on
  auth.register_rate_limit.lockout_seconds: a built-in value (3600)
  auth.register_rate_limit.max_attempts: a built-in value (5)
  auth.register_rate_limit.window_seconds: a built-in value (3600)
  auth.registration.allowed_email_domains: still read until M3 (N35), not written: the registration policy becomes an administrator setting; until then ignoring it would open registration to every address
  auth.registration.blocked_email_domains: still read until M3 (N35), not written: the registration policy becomes an administrator setting; until then ignoring it would open registration to every address
  auth.registration.enabled: still read until M3 (N35), not written: the registration policy becomes an administrator setting; until then ignoring it would reopen closed registration
  auth.registration.require_invite: still read until M3 (N35), not written: the registration policy becomes an administrator setting; until then ignoring it would drop the invite requirement
  cache.driver: nothing reads it; the cache is in memory
  cache.redis_db: nothing reads it; the cache is in memory
  cache.redis_host: nothing reads it; the cache is in memory
  cache.redis_password: nothing reads it; the cache is in memory
  cache.redis_port: nothing reads it; the cache is in memory
  env: Control always runs as production (its only effect was requiring jwt.secret, which is now derived); start a development instance with -debug
  forward_runtime.backend: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.clean_agent.action_timeout_seconds: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.clean_agent.heartbeat_interval_seconds: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
