  forward_runtime.latency.concurrency: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.latency.dial_timeout: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.latency.dials: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.latency.error_log_interval: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.latency.idle_poll_interval: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.latency.poll_interval: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.latency.retention_days: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.nodex.base_url: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.nodex.timeout_seconds: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  forward_runtime.nodex.token: the flux forward runtime (gost, NodeX, Ansible and the clean agent) was removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  frontend.enable: still read until M2 (P11), not written: serves the web app from frontend.path until the web app is built into the binary
  frontend.path: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the web app's directory until the web app is built into the binary
  frontend.port: still read until M2 (P11), not written: a second plain listener of tls.mode external while listen is unset; config rewrite does not carry it, point the reverse proxy at listen
  grpc.api_token: the legacy administrator token of the v2board gRPC services, which are removed; the key does nothing, so remove it
  grpc.enabled: still read until M2 (P11), not written: turns the gRPC listener on without domain; with domain it always runs
  grpc.host: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the gRPC listener's address, until it listens on every address
  grpc.port: the default (50051)
  jwt.expire: a built-in value (86400 seconds)
  jwt.secret: a template value: derived from the root key from now on
  log.file_path: nothing reads it; Control logs to standard output
  log.level: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the JSON log level, until the container files are removed; -debug turns on debug logging
  log.max_age: nothing reads it
  log.max_backups: nothing reads it
  log.max_size: nothing reads it
  log.output: nothing reads it; Control logs to standard output
  plugins.control_execution_enabled: the built-in packages always run; Control starts their hosts at every start
  plugins.control_host_artifact_dir: still read until M2 (P11), not written: where package hosts' files are kept, until the systemd unit gives Control its directories
  plugins.control_host_request_timeout: a built-in value (30s)
  plugins.control_host_runtime_dir: still read until M2 (P11), not written: where package hosts' sockets live, until the systemd unit gives Control its runtime directory
  plugins.control_host_startup_timeout: a built-in value (5s)
  plugins.control_host_websocket_session_timeout: a built-in value (24h)
  plugins.control_poll_interval: a built-in value (5s)
  plugins.dispatch_enabled: Agent plugin dispatch is off until the Agent release manifest brings the Agent plugins (M4)
  plugins.dispatch_poll_interval: Agent plugin dispatch is off until the Agent release manifest brings the Agent plugins (M4)
  plugins.identity_bootstrap_package_dir: still read until M2 (P11), not written: imports identity-platform into a development binary that embeds no packages; a release binary ignores it
  plugins.official_public_key: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the key the built-in packages verify against (development builds sign with their own), until the package index carries it
  plugins.topology_execution_enabled: topology deployment execution is off until the Agent release manifest brings the Agent plugins (M4)
  plugins.topology_poll_interval: topology deployment execution is off until the Agent release manifest brings the Agent plugins (M4)
  server.cors.allow_credentials: a built-in value (false)
  server.cors.allowed_headers: a built-in value (Content-Type, Authorization, X-API-Key)
  server.cors.allowed_methods: a built-in value (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, OPTIONS, PATCH)
  server.cors.allowed_origins: a built-in value (any origin, without credentials)
  server.cors.max_age: a built-in value (86400)
  server.host: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the plain listener of tls.mode external while listen is unset; config rewrite does not carry it, set listen
  server.mode: release mode is built in; start a development instance with -debug
  server.port: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the plain listener of tls.mode external while listen is unset; config rewrite does not carry it, set listen
  server.read_timeout: a built-in value (30 seconds)
  server.trusted_proxies: still read until M2 (P11), not written: the reverse proxies of a container deployment; afterwards tls.mode acme trusts none and tls.mode external trusts loopback
  server.write_timeout: a built-in value (30 seconds)
  tls.cert_file: not used: tls.enable was off (or there is no domain to serve)
  tls.enable: TLS follows tls.mode
  tls.key_file: not used: tls.enable was off (or there is no domain to serve)

Notes:
  tls.mode external: the old file did not use ACME, so a reverse proxy keeps terminating TLS for the web side; its gRPC certificate becomes tls.cert_file
  tls.mode external: point the reverse proxy at 127.0.0.1:8080 for the whole panel (web, /api, subscriptions, /install): it is one listener now
